Syncthing
=========

This module publishes synchronized Office roots to two Syncthing servers.
Read-only users are configured on the Send Only server and read-write users on
the Send & Receive server.  Configure both REST APIs in ``trytond.conf``::

    [syncthing]
    send_only_url = https://syncthing-ro.example:8384
    send_only_api_key = secret
    # send_only_certificate_fingerprint = sha256:AA:BB:...
    send_receive_url = https://syncthing-rw.example:8384
    send_receive_api_key = secret
    # send_receive_certificate_fingerprint = sha256:AA:BB:...
    timeout = 10
    verify_ssl = true
    # ca_file = /etc/ssl/private/syncthing-ca.pem

By default HTTPS certificates are verified against the system trust store, or
against ``ca_file`` when configured.  Set ``verify_ssl = false`` to accept any
certificate.  As a safer alternative for self-signed certificates, configure
the SHA-256 fingerprint independently for each server.  A configured
fingerprint takes precedence over CA verification and is checked before the
API key is sent.

When ``verify_ssl`` is disabled, the server fingerprint is logged as a warning
on the first request made by each client, without sending the API key while the
certificate is inspected.

When CA verification fails, the server fingerprint is logged without sending
the API key.  It can then be configured through ``trytond.conf`` or through
the corresponding environment variable::

    TRYTOND_SYNCTHING__SEND_ONLY_CERTIFICATE_FINGERPRINT=sha256:AA:BB:...
    TRYTOND_SYNCTHING__SEND_RECEIVE_CERTIFICATE_FINGERPRINT=sha256:AA:BB:...

Restart every Tryton web and queue worker process after changing these values.

Users register their device ID, display name and optional addresses from their
Tryton preferences.  Changes enqueue an idempotent reconciliation of managed
folders and devices while preserving unrelated Syncthing configuration.

Syncthing metadata such as ``.stfolder``, ``.stignore``, ``.stversions`` and
temporary ``.syncthing.*`` files is excluded from filesystem events and full
file synchronization.
